      "statement": "For every stable raw quadruple with μC=0 define α=(z0B1−z1,z0B2−z2,z0J)^T and β=(−z0B2+z2,z0B1−z1,z0I). Prove βα=z0²μC, α sheaf-injective, β everywhere onto, torsion-free middle cohomology with canonical framing and Hilbert polynomial N binom(m+2,2)−k. Conversely reconstruct the quadruple from every framed sheaf by the prior diagonal/vanishing theorem and prove inverse equivalence modulo GL, including families and tangent maps. Local freeness is equivalent to costability, so the regular locus is exactly the locally-free sheaf locus. Prove exact torus-equivariance in the dual-framing convention. No positive-FI identification with ordinary ASD is asserted.",
