## Scope and statement of the boundary

The category develops non-Abelian gauge theory, effective field theory,
supersymmetry, supersymmetric localization, BPS sectors, generalized global
symmetries, defects, and anomalies. It starts from reusable mathematical and
physical interfaces, makes missing prerequisites visible, and separates exact
conditional deductions from adopted models, formal perturbation theory,
regularized examples, unresolved questions, and empirical reports.

The existing `quantum-field-theory` and `quantum-field-theory-mathematics`
categories remain the suppliers for their exact published interfaces. The new
physics A/B pairs are assigned to `advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry`; new pure
mathematical suppliers use the existing `quantum-field-theory-mathematics`
category. A planned math interface remains a planning prerequisite, not a
