H1(L; O(−2)) = C so the restriction of χ to lines gives a function Fχ on Ω. More
precisely, there is a natural isomorphism of H1(L, KL) with C where KL is the
canonical line bundle of L. So to deﬁne Fχ we need to specify an isomorphism
of KL with O(−2)|L. If L = P(S) this is the same as a trivialisation of Λ2S.
